{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":42499,"duration_api_ms":42478,"num_turns":1,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Applied both pending amendments. Amendment 1: Replaced the tautological `per_guild_monod_uses_concentration_not_total` test in cycling.rs. The old test computed `tan_c = tan_total / volume_l` where `tan_total = tan_conc * volume_l`, so `tan_c == tan_conc` by construction — comparing `monod(tan_c, k)` with `monod(tan_conc, k)` was always an identity. The new test creates two TankState instances with the same total nutrient mass (TAN=30.0 mg) but different volumes (10 L vs 100 L), calls the production `step_nitrogen_cycle()` on both, and asserts the smaller tank (10× higher concentration) consumes more TAN due to stronger Monod limitation (small_tan_consumed > large_tan_consumed * 1.5). DOC is kept minimal (1.0 mg) so nitrification dominates over decomposer TAN production from mineralization. Amendment 2: Strengthened `loader_range_diagnostics_use_explicit_warning_lines` in tank_data/src/lib.rs from a single `contains(\\\"warning: preset...\\\")` check to four content assertions verifying: (1) preset/category identifier, (2) parameter name \\\"aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l\\\", (3) out-of-range value \\\"200\\\", and (4) valid range bounds \\\"0.1\\\" and \\\"5\\\". Each assertion includes a debug message showing the actual diagnostic string on failure.\",\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"Pre-existing test failure shrimp_population::shrimp_removal_validation (InvariantViolation on animal.egg_cohort_count_total) — confirmed fails without task changes, unrelated to gas exchange or nitrogen cycle\",\n    \"Pre-existing test failures depth_light_attenuation::shallow_vs_deep_200h_plant_growth and shallow_vs_deep_algae_competition — file was added by another task (tanksim-6e5.2.3.5) after our checkpoint 31e76a3, entirely unrelated to this task\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Read cycling.rs:1065-1175 